.el .ds Aq '
.TH whittle 1  "whittle 0.1.1" 
.SH NAME
whittle \- Tag\-aware long\-read trimmer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwhittle\fR [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-in\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-out\-format\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-ordered\fR] [\fB\-\-fastq\-tags\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-compression\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-summary\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-min\-length\fR] [\fB\-L\fR|\fB\-\-max\-length\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-min\-qual\fR] [\fB\-Q\fR|\fB\-\-max\-qual\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-min\-gc\fR] [\fB\-G\fR|\fB\-\-max\-gc\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-qual\-mode\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-head\-crop\fR] [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-tail\-crop\fR] [\fB\-\-qual\-trim\fR] [\fB\-\-qual\-best\-segment\fR] [\fB\-\-qual\-split\fR] [\fB\-\-qual\-split\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-update\-moves\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-adapter\-fasta\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-preset\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-error\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-end\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-ends\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-sample\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-infer\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-infer\-policy\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tag\-aware long\-read trimmer
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SETUP
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-input\fR \fI<INPUT>\fR
Input FASTQ\-family file, unaligned BAM, or directory; \- means stdin. Defaults to stdin
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output file, whose extension selects the format; \- means stdout. Defaults to stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-format\fR \fI<IN_FORMAT>\fR
Force the input format instead of detecting it from the path or stream
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fastq: Plain FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-gz: gzip\-compressed FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-bgz: BGZF\-compressed FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
bam: Unaligned BAM
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-out\-format\fR \fI<OUT_FORMAT>\fR
Force the output format instead of selecting it from the output path
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fastq: Plain FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-gz: gzip\-compressed FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-bgz: BGZF\-compressed FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
bam: Unaligned BAM
.RE
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<THREADS>\fR
Worker threads, at least 1; values above the CPU count are clamped to it. Defaults to all detected CPUs
.TP
\fB\-\-ordered\fR
Write records in input order when running with more than one thread. Without it, records are written as they finish, which is faster and uses less memory but is not reproducible between runs
.TP
\fB\-\-fastq\-tags\fR \fI<FASTQ_TAGS>\fR [default: all]
BAM auxiliary tags copied into BAM\-to\-FASTQ headers: all, none, or a list such as MM,ML,RG. Defaults to all
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-compression\-level\fR \fI<COMPRESSION_LEVEL>\fR
DEFLATE compression level (0\-9) for compressed output: bgzf for BAM and .bgz, gzip for FASTQ.gz. Lower levels are faster and produce larger files. Ignored for plain FASTQ. Defaults to 4 for gzip FASTQ and 6 for BGZF
.TP
\fB\-\-summary\-json\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write a machine\-readable JSON run summary (counters plus the resolved settings) to this path. Written even under \-\-quiet
.SH LOGGING
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase logging detail: \-v is debug, \-vv is trace (at most two). Overridden by WHITTLE_LOG
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Silence progress and info output; warnings and errors still print. Conflicts with \-v and \-\-progress
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
Progress reporting, independent of the log level: auto selects a bar on a terminal and periodic lines otherwise; bar and plain force one form; none disables progress and keeps the banner and summary. A bar falls back to lines under \-v or WHITTLE_LOG. Defaults to auto
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A bar on a terminal, periodic lines otherwise
.IP \(bu 2
bar: The animated bar, unless \-v or WHITTLE_LOG asks for log lines
.IP \(bu 2
plain: Always periodic lines, never a bar
.IP \(bu 2
none: No progress reporting; the banner and summary still print
.RE
.SH FILTERING
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-min\-length\fR \fI<MIN_LENGTH>\fR [default: 1]
Minimum post\-trim segment length. Defaults to 1
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-max\-length\fR \fI<MAX_LENGTH>\fR
Maximum post\-trim segment length
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-min\-qual\fR \fI<MIN_QUAL>\fR [default: 0]
Minimum post\-trim read quality under \-\-qual\-mode. Defaults to 0
.TP
\fB\-Q\fR, \fB\-\-max\-qual\fR \fI<MAX_QUAL>\fR [default: 1000]
Maximum post\-trim read quality under \-\-qual\-mode. Defaults to 1000
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-min\-gc\fR \fI<MIN_GC>\fR
Minimum post\-trim GC fraction (0 to 1)
.TP
\fB\-G\fR, \fB\-\-max\-gc\fR \fI<MAX_GC>\fR
Maximum post\-trim GC fraction (0 to 1)
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-qual\-mode\fR \fI<QUAL_MODE>\fR [default: mean]
Read\-quality summary used by the quality filters. Defaults to mean
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
mean: Average error probabilities, then convert the result back to Phred Q
.IP \(bu 2
arithmetic: Take the arithmetic mean of the per\-base Phred scores
.IP \(bu 2
median: Take the median per\-base Phred score
.RE
.SH TRIMMING
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-head\-crop\fR \fI<HEAD_CROP>\fR [default: 0]
Remove this many bases from the 5\*(Aq end before other trimming. Defaults to 0
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-tail\-crop\fR \fI<TAIL_CROP>\fR [default: 0]
Remove this many bases from the 3\*(Aq end before other trimming. Defaults to 0
.TP
\fB\-\-qual\-trim\fR \fI<QUAL_TRIM>\fR
Trim low\-quality bases from both ends until each boundary reaches Q
.TP
\fB\-\-qual\-best\-segment\fR \fI<QUAL_BEST_SEGMENT>\fR
Keep the longest contiguous segment whose bases are all at least Q
.TP
\fB\-\-qual\-split\fR \fI<QUAL_SPLIT>\fR
Split at low\-quality runs below Q and keep the surviving segments
.TP
\fB\-\-qual\-split\-window\fR \fI<QUAL_SPLIT_WINDOW>\fR [default: 1]
Tolerate low\-quality runs shorter than this many bases when splitting. Requires \-\-qual\-split. Defaults to 1
.TP
\fB\-\-update\-moves\fR
Keep ONT signal tags consistent through trimming (slice mv, update ts, ns, sp and pi) for signal\-aware tools such as Remora and Clair3 v2, instead of dropping them. BAM\-to\-BAM only
.SH "ADAPTER TRIMMING"
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-adapter\-fasta\fR \fI<ADAPTER_FASTA>\fR
Adapter FASTA; each sequence must be at least 11 bp. Enables adapter trimming
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-preset\fR \fI<ADAPTER_PRESET>\fR [default: none]
Built\-in ONT adapter catalog. Enables adapter trimming. Defaults to none
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
none: Do not load a built\-in adapter catalog
.IP \(bu 2
ont: Load the built\-in Oxford Nanopore adapter and barcode catalog
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-error\-rate\fR \fI<ADAPTER_ERROR_RATE>\fR
End\-match tolerance as a fraction of adapter length; interior splits use half. Requires an adapter source. Defaults to 0.2
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-end\-size\fR \fI<ADAPTER_END_SIZE>\fR
Bases at each read end searched for a terminal adapter. Requires an adapter source. Defaults to 150
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-ends\-only\fR
Trim adapters at read ends only; never split on interior adapters
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-sample\fR \fI<ADAPTER_SAMPLE>\fR
Reads sampled for preset detection or ab\-initio inference; inference requires at least 100. Requires an adapter source. Defaults to 0 for preset detection and 40000 for inference
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-infer\fR [\fI<ADAPTER_INFER>\fR]
Discover adapters de novo. Report prints the inferred FASTA and exits without writing read output. Defaults to trim when given no value
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
trim: Trim reads with the inferred sequences
.IP \(bu 2
report: Print inferred FASTA to stdout and do not write read output
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-infer\-policy\fR \fI<ADAPTER_INFER_POLICY>\fR [default: conservative]
Trust policy for inferred consensuses. Aggressive uses the complete consensus and permits splitting unless ends\-only is set. Defaults to conservative
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
conservative: Use a short end\-facing anchor and disable inferred interior splitting
.IP \(bu 2
aggressive: Use the complete recurrent consensus and allow interior splitting
.RE
